# Maps into a henselian local ring (Stacks tags 08HQ, 08HR)

Let `R → S` be a ring map with `S` henselian local with maximal ideal `m_S`, and
set `p = R ∩ m_S`, the contraction of `m_S` along `R → S`. Given an étale ring map
`R → A`, a prime `q` of `A` lying over `p`, and a `κ(p)`-algebra map
`τ : κ(q) → κ(m_S) = S/m_S`, there is a unique homomorphism of `R`-algebras
`f : A → S` such that `q = f⁻¹(m_S)` and `f` induces `τ` on residue fields.

The argument passes to the étale `S`-algebra `B := S ⊗[R] A`. The residue datum
`(q, τ)` cuts out a prime `𝔫` of `B` lying over `m_S` with `κ(𝔫) = κ(m_S)`, and the
base-change bijection `Hom_R(A, S) ≃ Hom_S(B, S)` turns the two conditions on `f`
into the single condition `σ⁻¹(m_S) = 𝔫` on an `S`-algebra retraction
`σ : B →ₐ[S] S`. Such a `σ` exists and is unique because `B` is standard étale near
`𝔫`, so `σ` amounts to a root of a polynomial over `S` with unit derivative, and
Hensel's lemma produces exactly one such root.

## Conventions

Throughout, "ring" means commutative ring with unit and all ring maps are unital.
The structure map `φ : R → S` is encoded as `algebraMap R S` via the `Algebra R S`
instance.

* A henselian local ring is Mathlib's `HenselianLocalRing S`, which packages that
  `S` is local and that Hensel's lemma holds in its root-lifting form.
* An étale ring map is `Algebra.Etale R A`.
* For a prime `I` of a commutative ring, `Ideal.ResidueField I` is the residue
  field `κ(I) = Frac(·/I)`. For the henselian local ring `S` we use the residue
  field of its maximal ideal `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S`, which is canonically
  `S/m_S`. Given a ring map `f : R →+* S` and primes with `I = comap f J`, the
  induced field map `κ(I) → κ(J)` is `Ideal.ResidueField.map I J f h`.
* The contraction `p = R ∩ m_S` is the ideal
  `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S).comap (algebraMap R S)`. As the contraction of a
  prime ideal it is automatically prime, so it is inlined directly and no separate
  primality hypothesis is needed.
* `q` lies over `p` is the equality `q.comap (algebraMap R A) = p`.

That `τ` is a `κ(p)`-algebra map is expressed as a commuting triangle: precomposing
`τ` with the induced map `κ(p) → κ(q)` gives the induced map `κ(p) → κ(m_S)`. That
`f` induces `τ` on residue fields is the equality
`Ideal.ResidueField.map q m_S f h = τ`, where `h : comap f m_S = q`.

Tag 08HR is the same statement with `R → A` only *ind-étale*: `A` a filtered colimit of étale
`R`-algebras, `(CommAlgCat.etale R).ind (CommAlgCat.of R A)`. Writing `A = colim_j A_j`, the
residue datum `(q, τ)` contracts to a residue datum `(q_j, τ_j)` on each étale stage `A_j`, the
étale case produces a unique `f_j : A_j → S`, and that uniqueness is what makes the `f_j`
compatible; the colimit then glues them into `f`.

## Main results

* `existsUnique_algHom_henselian_of_residue_datum`: the étale case, in terms of
  `Ideal.ResidueField.map`.
* `Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.exists_unique_algHom_etale`: the étale case again, in terms of the
  `κ(p)`-algebra data `residueFieldMapBase`, `residueFieldMapFib` and `InducesResidueMap`
  in which the ind-étale case is stated.
* `Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.algHom`: the ind-étale case, Tag 08HR — the lift itself, with
  `Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.algHom_spec` for its two defining properties and
  `Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.algHom_unique` for its uniqueness.

## Implementation notes

*The rings may live in independent universes.* The ind-étale presentation is taken in the common
ambient universe of `R` and `A`, with apex `ULift A`, while `S` remains arbitrary. The colimit is
therefore not directly available for descending into `S`.
The two facts the gluing needs are supplied instead by
`Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.exists_algHom_comp_ι_eq` and
`Stacks.Henselian.EtaleLifting.algHom_eq_of_comp_ι_eq`, which descend into a `Type u` model of the
subalgebra of `S` generated by the images, resp. descend into the equalizer of two competing maps,
both of which *are* objects of `CommAlgCat.{u} R`.

## Parts

* `EtaleLifting.HenselianRetraction`: the étale case of Tag 08HQ via henselian retractions.
* `EtaleLifting.IndEtale`: the ind-étale case, Tag 08HR.
* `EtaleLifting.SolutionsRigidity`: injectivity on solutions of an étale system (Tag 04GX).
* `EtaleLifting.SolutionsBijection`: surjectivity and the bijection on solutions (Tag 04GX).

